{"ref":"BDB, מֶרְכָּבָה","hw":"מֶרְכָּבָה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מֶרְכָּבָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. chariot</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 4:15\" href=\"/Judges.4.15\">Ju 4:15</a> +, cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִרְכֶּ֫בֶת</span> †<a data-ref=\"Genesis 41:43\" href=\"/Genesis.41.43\">Gn 41:43</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מֶרְכַּבְתּוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 46:29\" href=\"/Genesis.46.29\">46:29</a> +; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַרְכָּבוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 6:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.6.1\">Zc 6:1</a> +; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַרְכְּבוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:11\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.11\">2 K 23:11</a> +, -<span dir=\"rtl\">בֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:4\" href=\"/Exodus.15.4\">Ex 15:4</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַרְכְּבֹתֶיךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 5:10\" href=\"/Micah.5.10\">Mi 5:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 3:8\" href=\"/Habakkuk.3.8\">Hb 3:8</a>, etc.;—<em>chariot</em> (often ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">סוּס(ים)</span>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 8:11\" href=\"/I_Samuel.8.11\">1 S 8:11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">פָרָשִׁים</span>): especially war-chariot, Egypt., <a data-ref=\"Exodus 14:25\" href=\"/Exodus.14.25\">Ex 14:25</a> (J), <a data-ref=\"Genesis 15:4\" href=\"/Genesis.15.4\">15:4</a> (song), <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 14:8\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.14.8\">2 Ch 14:8</a>; from <em>Muṣri</em> in N. Syriac (according to Wkl., v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, מִצְרַ֫יִם\" href=\"/BDB,_מִצְרַ֫יִם\", dir=\"rtl\">מצרים</a> <em>ad</em> fin., cf. Kit <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 10:18\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.10.18\">1 K 10:28</a> Benz<sup>1b.</sup>) <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.29\">1 K 10:29</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 1:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.1.17\">2 Ch 1:17</a>; Can., <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:6\" href=\"/Joshua.11.6\">Jos 11:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:9\" href=\"/Joshua.11.9\">9</a> (JE), <a data-ref=\"Judges 4:15\" href=\"/Judges.4.15\">Ju 4:15</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">רֶכֶב</span>), <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:28\" href=\"/Judges.5.28\">5:28</a> (‖ id.); Assyrian, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 2:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.2.7\">Is 2:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:2\" href=\"/Nahum.3.2\">Na 3:2</a>; foe from north <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.13\">Je 4:13</a>, nations in gen. <a data-ref=\"Haggai 2:22\" href=\"/Haggai.2.22\">Hg 2:22</a>; Isr. and Jud. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 20:33\" href=\"/I_Kings.20.33\">1 K 20:33</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:35\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.35\">22:35</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 18:34\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.18.34\">2 Ch 18:34</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:27\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.27\">2 K 9:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 10:15\" href=\"/II_Kings.10.15\">10:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 35:24\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.35.24\">2 Ch 35:24</a>; <a data-ref=\"Micah 5:10\" href=\"/Micah.5.10\">Mi 5:10</a>; fig. of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>’s chariots <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 66:15\" href=\"/Isaiah.66.15\">Is 66:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 3:8\" href=\"/Habakkuk.3.8\">Hb 3:8</a>, cf. (in vision) <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 6:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.6.1\">Zc 6:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 6:2\" href=\"/Zechariah.6.2\">2</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 6:3\" href=\"/Zechariah.6.3\">3</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> for dignity and display <a data-ref=\"Genesis 41:43\" href=\"/Genesis.41.43\">Gn 41:43</a> (E), <a data-ref=\"Genesis 46:29\" href=\"/Genesis.46.29\">46:29</a> (J), <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 8:11\" href=\"/I_Samuel.8.11\">1 S 8:11</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 15:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.15.1\">2 S 15:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 5:21\" href=\"/II_Kings.5.21\">2 K 5:21</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 5:26\" href=\"/II_Kings.5.26\">26</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מַרְכְּבוֹת כְּבוֹדֶ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 22:18\" href=\"/Isaiah.22.18\">Is 22:18</a> (iron.); used in flight <a data-ref=\"I Kings 12:18\" href=\"/I_Kings.12.18\">1 K 12:18</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 10:18\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.10.18\">2 Ch 10:18</a>, <a data-ref=\"Micah 1:13\" href=\"/Micah.1.13\">Mi 1:13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מַרְכְּבוֹת הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:11\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.11\">2 K 23:11</a> (idolatrous); <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמּ׳ הַכְּרוּבִים</span> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">מִרְכֶּבֶת הַכּ׳</span>, 𝔊 Benz) <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 28:18\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.28.18\">1 Ch 28:18</a> (on this conception of cherubim in temple v. Benz); <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> in similes: <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּמַעֲשֵׂה אוֹפַן הַמּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:33\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.33\">1 K 7:33</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּקוֹל מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Joel 2:5\" href=\"/Joel.2.5\">Jo 2:5</a>; obscure <span dir=\"rtl\">מַר׳ עַמִּי נָדִיב</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:12\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.12\">Ct 6:12</a> <em>chariots of my people, a prince</em> (?)—<span dir=\"rtl\">בֵּית מַרְכָּבוֹת</span> v. p. 112.","next":"BDB, רֵכָה","prev":"BDB, מֶרְכָּב²"}